{
  "id": "topographic-organization",
  "term": "topographic organization",
  "definition": "Topographic organization is the orderly layout of sensory cortex so that nearby brain areas correspond to nearby parts of the sensory surface, such as neighboring points on the retina or neighboring whiskers. This arrangement can also include finer maps in which nearby neurons respond to similar stimulus features, like movement direction.",
